.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-mora 1  "git-mora 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
git\-mora \- Small helpers for agent branches, workflow tags, and informational topics
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit mora\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Small helpers for agent branches, workflow tags, and informational topics.
.PP
Names: agent branch   agent/<agent\-id>/<target>/<attempt\-id> workflow tags  pending|merge|discard/<target>/<attempt\-id> topic index    refs/topics/<topic\-id>
.PP
Mora never moves an existing tag to different code, runs reviews, chooses integrations, or publishes. Only requested branches/tags, topic blobs/refs, and optional worktree\-local topic context are persisted.
.PP
Exit status: 0 success (including no\-op or empty list), 1 operation failed, 2 invalid arguments, 3 wait timed out.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
git\-mora\-branch(1)
Create a uniquely named agent branch and print its name
.TP
git\-mora\-tag(1)
Tag the current attempt as pending, merge, or discard
.TP
git\-mora\-list(1)
List matching local branches and tags, then exit
.TP
git\-mora\-listen(1)
Watch for matching tags and branches being created
.TP
git\-mora\-wait(1)
Wait for matching tags or branches to exist or disappear
.TP
git\-mora\-hook(1)
Run a topic\-tracking adapter from an existing Git hook
.TP
git\-mora\-topic(1)
Create, inspect, and update informational topic associations
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
